flowchart LR
    In["<b>1. frame enters bridge port</b><br/>skb carries src/dst MAC, VLAN, and ingress port<br/><b>handoff:</b> bridge must learn before it forwards<br/><b>state:</b> skb is associated with a br_port"]

    Learn["<b>2. learn source</b><br/>record src MAC/VLAN to ingress port and refresh age<br/><b>handoff:</b> destination decision can use the updated FDB<br/><b>state:</b> reverse traffic can become known unicast"]

    Policy["<b>3. bridge policy</b><br/>check port state, STP, VLAN filtering, and local delivery cases<br/><b>handoff:</b> only forwarding ports may send frames onward<br/><b>state:</b> frame is allowed, locally consumed, or dropped"]

    Lookup["<b>4. destination lookup</b><br/>search FDB for dst MAC/VLAN<br/><b>handoff:</b> hit selects one port, miss/broadcast selects flood set<br/><b>state:</b> egress port list is known"]

    Egress["<b>5. egress copies</b><br/>queue one skb for known unicast or clones for flood<br/><b>handoff:</b> selected ports pass frames to qdisc/driver<br/><b>state:</b> one or many egress skbs"]

    Drop["<b>drop / consume</b><br/>no egress frame"]

    In --> Learn --> Policy --> Lookup --> Egress
    Policy -. blocked or local .-> Drop

    classDef br fill:#fef3c7,stroke:#d97706,stroke-width:2px
    classDef ok fill:#dcfce7,stroke:#16a34a,stroke-width:2px
    classDef bad fill:#fee2e2,stroke:#dc2626,stroke-width:2px
    class In,Learn,Policy,Lookup br
    class Egress ok
    class Drop bad
